msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/is-it-encapsulated.md:21
msgid "// Validation checks...\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/is-it-encapsulated.md:26
msgid "// ‼️\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/is-it-encapsulated.md:43
msgid ""
"`DerefMut` allows users to get a mutable reference to the wrapped value."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/is-it-encapsulated.md:45
msgid ""
"The mutable reference can be used to modify the underlying data in ways that "
"may violate the invariants enforced by `Username::new`!"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/is-it-encapsulated.md:48
msgid ""
"When auditing the API surface of a newtype, you can narrow down the review "
"scope to methods and traits that provide mutable access to the underlying "
"data."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/is-it-encapsulated.md:52
msgid "Remind students of privacy boundaries."
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern/is-it-encapsulated.md:54
msgid ""
"In particular, functions and methods defined in the same module of the "
"newtype can access its underlying data directly. If possible, move the "
"newtype definition to its own separate module to reduce the scope of the "
"audit."
msgstr ""
